  <question type="stack">
    <name>
      <text>Find the Volume of the  Cylinder-q3</text>
    </name>
    <questiontext format="html">
      <text><![CDATA[<p>Use the method of cylinders to determine the volume of the solid obtained by rotating the region bounded by \({@eqn_1@}\) and \({@eqn_2@}\) about the line \({@line@}\) which is given by the sketch below.</p>
<p>
[[jsxgraph]] 
 var board = JXG.JSXGraph.initBoard(divid, {
            boundingbox: [-12, 3, 24, -12],
            keepaspectratio: true,
            showCopyright: false,
            axis: true,
            showNavigation: true
        });
 var function1 = board.create('functiongraph', ['{#line_x#}',  {#line_x1#},{#line_x2#}], { name: '{#line#}', withlabel: true });
  var function3 = board.create('functiongraph', [function(y){return y*y-{#const_1#};}, -10, 10],{name:'y^2 - {#const_1#}', withLabel:true, strokeColor:'black'});
    var function2 = board.create('functiongraph', [function(y){return {#const_2-coeff_y*y#};}, -10, 10],{name:'{#const_2-coeff_y *y#}', withLabel:true, strokeColor:'black'});
make_filled_curve(board, [function1, function3, function2], { strokeWidth: 3, fillColor: 'yellow', fillOpacity: 0.3 });
 
       
[[/jsxgraph]]
</p>
<p>\(V= \) [[input:ans1]] [[validation:ans1]][[feedback:prt1]]</p>]]></text>
    </questiontext>
    <generalfeedback format="html">
      <text><![CDATA[<p><h3>Worked solution</h3></p>
<p>Recall that, by using the method of cylinders, the volume of the solid generated by a region bounded by the lines \(\displaystyle y=a\) and \(\displaystyle y=b\), which is revolved about the axis \(\displaystyle y=c\) is given by</p>

<p>\(\displaystyle V=2 \pi \int_{a}^{b}(y-c)f(y) dy,\) and radius \(\displaystyle r=y-c\)</p>
<p>The values \(a\) and \(b\) are obtained from the intersection points as shown in the sketch. So we set the two equations \(x={@eqn_1@}\) and \(x={@eqn_2@}\) equal and solve it.</p>
<p> 
    \( \displaystyle
    \begin{align}
    {@eqn_1@}={@eqn_2@} &amp; \Longleftrightarrow {@eqn_3@}=0 \\
    &amp;\Longleftrightarrow {@solve@} \\
    \end{align}
    \)
</p>
<p>For this problem, \(\displaystyle a={@min@},b={@max@},r={@Radius@}\) and \(f(y)=({@eqn_1@})-({@eqn_2@})={@Width@}\).</p>
<p>Recall that the value of the volume must be positive. When \(V\) is negative, you pick its absolute value.</p>
<p>Therefore,</p>
<p>
    \(\displaystyle
    \begin{align}
    V &amp;=2 \pi \int_{{@min@}}^{{@max@}}({@Radius@}) \cdot ({@Width@})\,dy \\
    &amp;= 2 \pi \int_{{@min@}}^{{@max@}}({@Area_y_1@})\,dy \\
    &amp;=\left [ {@Vol_1@} \right ]_{{@min@}}^{{@max@}} \\
    &amp;={@ta@}
    \end{align}
    \)
</p>]]></text>
    </generalfeedback>
